experiment: hush
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 900000. derived: §60. WHAT CLOSES THE LARYNX? §59a found every arm losing 55-80% of
  its probes between e7 and e8, keyed to ABSOLUTE ticks, with the PINNED arms
  -- whose index cannot collapse -- falling silent hardest. It read the cause
  off `probe_why == 1` and published "no voiced frame at all". But that flag
  is `probe_fn == 0`, and `probe_fn` counts frames that are BOTH voiced AND
  above kAmplitudeFloor: a gate that never opened and a voice too quiet to
  score are different mechanisms, and the published reading asserts one
  conjunct of two. The primary splits them -- q = QUIET / (SIL + QUIET) in e8,
  bounds 0.20 and 0.80 fixed before the run, 8.1 SE of binomial headroom.
  Secondary 1 asks whether the larynx threshold has reached its clamp, as
  `ipctx` measured at 3.4M on another protocol, and records up front that NOT
  SATURATED refutes only the saturation story and not the homeostat.
  INSTRUMENTATION ONLY: seven per-probe vectors and two pure reads. `ip_rate`
  is a refused knob and no arm here touches it. The free control hardcodes
  §59a's ledger and checks 160 integers, so any perturbation breaks the run.
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §60. The e7->e8 silence cliff. `probe_why == 1` is
                    `probe_fn == 0`, and `probe_fn` counts frames that are
                    BOTH voiced AND above kAmplitudeFloor (0.45). §59a read
                    that conjunction as one term and published "no voiced
                    frame at all". WHICH CONJUNCT FAILS?
  the primary       q = QUIET / (SIL + QUIET) in e8, where SIL is a probe
                    with no voiced frame and QUIET one with voiced frames
                    that were all too soft. q <= 0.20 VOICING, q >= 0.80
                    AMPLITUDE, between MIXED. Bounds fixed before the run.
  not power-bound   at §59a's smallest e8 count (n 182) a share's binomial
                    SE is at worst 0.0371, so the bounds sit 8.1 SE from
                    0.5 and MIXED fires below 1e-6 unless the quantity IS a
                    mixture. The bands are wide because they can afford to
                    be, not as a hedge.
  secondary 1       is the regulator out of range? pinned share of the
                    larynx at >= 0.999 x threshold_max (4.00) in e8.
                    `ipctx` read 0.31 at gain 0.10 over 3.4M on another
                    protocol. >= 0.05 SATURATED, < 0.05 NOT SATURATED.
  AND ITS LIMIT     registered before the run: NOT SATURATED does NOT
                    refute the homeostat. A threshold that rises without
                    reaching its clamp can close the voicing gate on its
                    own; only the SATURATION story dies.
  the free control  §59a's ledger is hardcoded here. 3 arms x 8 eighths x 5
                    integers on r 0..35, plus T1.ORACLE on r 0..11 -- 160
                    integers that ANY perturbation of the session breaks.
  measures only     `ip_rate` is a REFUSED knob (the arm that answers 2.7x
                    more trials learns 6x less). No arm here touches it.
  session           150.0 s of simulated life x 144 sessions, 4 arms x 36 reps
  instrument        hush   trial seed 0000000001354769   144 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  INDEX SOURCE      5 (vision-derived), set PER JOB below together with
                    context_slots = 2 and ctx_proto_gate = 2. The base
                    genome's own `context_source` is 0 and is NOT what
                    these arms run.

  LIVENESS. completed sessions per arm:  T1.RET 36/36  T1.RET.D 36/36  T1.ORACLE.D 36/36  T1.ORACLE 36/36

